Real coefficients for the element routines in this add-on.

-----------------------------------
1   A: the constant cross sectional area of the truss or beam.

2   Emod: the elastic modulus

3   Iz: the constant second moment of area with respect to the neutral (local)
    z-axis, commonly denoted by just I in 1D and 2D problems. Also Izz for 3D
    beam problems.
    NOTE: the (local) x-axis is along the beam.

4   Constant scalar distributed load q. Available for 1D beams only.

5-7 (qx,qy,qz): constant distributed load q. For a truss element the total
    force on an elements is equally transferred to the nodes.

8-10 (Zx,Zy,Zz): vector pointing in the local z-axis direction. Only relevant
    for 3D beam elements. Defining the unit vector nz = Z/|Z|, the unit vector
    in the direction of the local y-axis is ny = nz x e. Here, e is the unit
    vector in the local x-axis direction. The positive direction of the x-as 
    is given by local beam coordinate s, which starts from the first end node
    (s=0) and ends at the final end nod (s=L).

11  Iyy: the constant second moment of area with respect to the neutral (local)
    y-axis. Only needed for 3D beams.

12  Izy: the constant product moment of area with respect to the neutral (local)
    z and y-axis. Only needed for 3D beams.

13  J: the constant polar second moment of area. Only needed for 3D beams.

14  Gmod: the shear modulus

15-50 reserved for future use
